        "title": "Deep Research Agents: Automating Literature Review and Synthesis",
        "excerpt":"   “An LLM knows what it was trained on. A Research Agent knows what was published 5 minutes ago.”    Standard RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is brittle. It fetches the top-3 snippets and prays the answer is there. Deep Research Agents (like OpenAI’s Deep Research or Perplexity Pro) go further. They act like a human analyst:     They plan a search strategy.   They read multiple sources.   They follow links recursively.   They synthesize a report with citations.   This post explores the architecture of autonomous information gathering.      Related reading: Builds on The Era of AI Agents by applying it to the specific domain of knowledge discovery.      Chapter I: The Breadth vs Depth Trade-off   A research agent must balance:     Breadth: How many disparate queries to run? (“competitors to Nike”, “Nike financial reports”, “Nike recent scandals”)   Depth: How deep to click? (Search Result -&gt; Landing Page -&gt; PDF Report -&gt; Footnote).   The Recursive Algorithm  Most research agents use a DFS (Depth-First Search) approach with a “satisfaction” stopping condition.   graph TD     Goal[User Goal: Analyze Competitors] --&gt; Plan[Generate 3 Sub-Questions]     Plan --&gt; Q1[Q1: Who are they?]     Plan --&gt; Q2[Q2: Revenue?]     Plan --&gt; Q3[Q3: Strategy?]      Q1 --&gt; Search1[Search: 'Nike competitors']     Search1 --&gt; Read1[Read: Article 1]     Read1 --&gt; Follow[Follow Link: 'Adidas Annual Report']      Q2 --&gt; Search2[...]     Chapter II: The Architecture of Synthesis   Reading is easy. Writing is hard. How do you combine 10,000 words of scraped text into a 500-word cohesive summary?   Map-Reduce Summarization:     Map: Summarize each individual document into key facts relevant to the query.   Cluster: Group facts by theme (e.g., “Financials”, “Product”, “Legal”).   Reduce: Write a paragraph for each theme.   This avoids the “Lost in the Middle” phenomenon where LLMs forget the middle of a long context window.     Chapter III: Citation and Verification   The cardinal sin of research is hallucination. Research Agents must enforce Citation Tracking.   Every sentence in the final output must be back-traceable to a Source ID.     Bad: “Revenue grew 20%.”   Good: “Revenue grew 20% [Source: 10-K Report, Page 45].”   Implementation Tip: Force the model to generate XML tags &lt;cite id=\"1\"&gt; immediately after facts.     Chapter IV: Building a Toy Research Agent   import time  class ResearchAgent:     def __init__(self, topic):         self.topic = topic         self.knowledge_base = []      def step_1_plan(self):         print(f\"Planning research for: {self.topic}\")         # Mock LLM call to generating queries         return [f\"{self.topic} history\", f\"{self.topic} recent news\"]      def step_2_execute(self, queries):         for q in queries:             print(f\"Searching: {q}...\")             # Mock Search API             results = [{\"title\": f\"Article about {q}\", \"url\": \"http://example.com\"}]              for res in results:                 print(f\"  Reading: {res['title']}\")                 # Mock Scraper                 content = f\"Important fact about {q} found in {res['url']}\"                 self.knowledge_base.append(content)      def step_3_synthesize(self):         print(\"\\nSynthesizing Report...\")         full_context = \"\\n\".join(self.knowledge_base)         # Mock LLM Summarization         report = f\"## Report on {self.topic}\\nBased on {len(self.knowledge_base)} sources:\\n\"         for fact in self.knowledge_base:             report += f\"- {fact}\\n\"         return report  agent = ResearchAgent(\"Quantum Computing\") queries = agent.step_1_plan() agent.step_2_execute(queries) print(agent.step_3_synthesize())     Chapter V: Use Cases in Advertising   Why does an Ad Tech engineer care? Creative Strategy.   Instead of guessing what ads to write, a Research Agent can:     “Scan all competitor ads for ‘Running Shoes’ in the last month.”   “Identify the top 3 value propositions used (e.g., ‘Comfort’ vs ‘Speed’).”   “Find 1-star reviews on Amazon to identify user pain points.”   “Propose 5 new ad angles based on gaps.”   This turns “Deep Research” into “High-Converting Copy”.     Summary   Deep Research Agents automate the top of the funnel (Strategy). They don’t just find links; they synthesize knowledge. The next generation of CEOs will have a fleet of these agents reading the entire internet every morning.      “Knowledge is power. Synthesis is leverage.”    title: “Deep Research Agents: Automating Literature Review and Synthesis” date: 2025-12-01 categories:         Artificial Intelligence     Machine Learning tags:     agentic-ai     llm     research-agents            rag           ","categories": ["Artificial Intelligence","Machine Learning"],
        "tags": ["agentic-ai","llm","research-agents","rag"],
