        "title": "Funnel Tradeoffs in Advertising: Optimizing Awareness, Conversion, and Retention",
        "excerpt":"   “Performance marketing harvests existing demand. Brand marketing creates future demand. If you only harvest, you will starve.”    A common tragedy in Ad Tech:     CFO joins. Demands $ROAS \\ge 4.0$.   Marketing team cuts TV, YouTube, and “Brand Awareness” because they have low ROAS.   They shift budget to “Retargeting” (showing shoes to people who just looked at shoes).   Short term: ROAS skyrockets to $8.0$.   Long term: New user growth flatlines. The brand dies.   This post explores the Upper Funnel vs Lower Funnel problem and how to solve it mathematically.      Related reading: This connects Incrementality Testing with the strategic budgeting discussed in Online Bid Optimization.      Chapter I: The Funnel Physics   The funnel is a flow metrics problem.      Upper Funnel (Awareness): Low Probability of Conversion (pCVR), High Volume.   Lower Funnel (Conversion): High pCVR, Low Volume.   The Trap: Last-Touch Attribution gives 100% credit to the Lower Funnel (Search/Retargeting). The Upper Funnel (which introduced the user to the brand) gets 0 credit.     Chapter II: The “Performance Performance” vs “Brand Performance”   We need to split metrics.                  Stage       Metric       Measurement                       Lower Funnel       CPA, ROAS       Attribution / Click Cookies                 Upper Funnel       Lift in Search Volume, Brand Lift       Geo-Experiments / Surveys           The Correlation: \\(Volume(Search) \\propto Spend(Brand, t-30 \\text{days})\\) There is a lag. Spending on TV today increases Google Search volume next month.     Chapter III: Modeling the Tradeoff   We can model the total system revenue as a coupled differential equation or a multi-stage regression.   \\(NewUsers_t = \\alpha \\cdot BrandSpend_t + \\beta \\cdot NewUsers_{t-1}\\) \\(Conversions_t = \\gamma \\cdot NewUsers_t \\cdot PerfSpend_t\\)   If $BrandSpend \\to 0$, then $NewUsers \\to 0$. Eventually $Conversions \\to 0$, no matter how high $PerfSpend$ is.   Optimization with MMM  Marketing Mix Modeling (MMM) estimates the $\\alpha$ and $\\gamma$ parameters without needing user-level tracking.     Chapter IV: Python Simulator   Let’s simulate the creating vs harvesting dynamic.   import numpy as np import matplotlib.pyplot as plt  def simulate_business(weeks=52, brand_budget=1000, perf_budget=1000):     # Initial State     awareness_pool = 10000     revenue = []      for w in range(weeks):         # 1. Brand Marketing feeds the Awareness Pool         # Cost per Reach = $0.10         new_aware = (brand_budget / 0.10)         # Decay: 10% of people forget the brand every week         awareness_pool = awareness_pool * 0.9 + new_aware          # 2. Performance Marketing harvests the Awareness Pool         # Conversion Rate depends of Performance Spend         cvr = min(0.05, perf_budget / 100000)         conversions = awareness_pool * cvr          # Revenue ($50 per sale)         rev = conversions * 50         revenue.append(rev)      return revenue  # Scenario A: Balanced rev_balanced = simulate_business(brand_budget=5000, perf_budget=5000)  # Scenario B: All Performance (Harvest Strategy) rev_harvest = simulate_business(brand_budget=0, perf_budget=10000)  plt.plot(rev_balanced, label='Balanced') plt.plot(rev_harvest, label='All Performance') plt.legend() plt.title(\"The Death Spiral of Pure Performance\") plt.ylabel(\"Revenue\") plt.xlabel(\"Week\") # Result: 'All Performance' wins for 5 weeks, then crashes as awareness pool drains.     Chapter V: Agentic Optimization   In the Agentic Era, we don’t just set static budgets. An Allocator Agent monitors the “Health of the Funnel”.      Signal: “Brand Search Volume is down 10% YoY.”   Action: “Shift 20% of budget from Retargeting to Youtube Reach campaigns.”   This is Full-Funnel Automation.     Summary   The job of the CMO (and the algorithm) is to balance Efficiency (ROAS) and Growth (Reach).     Too much Efficiency = Shrinking Business.   Too much Growth = Bankruptcy.   The Sweet Spot = Using MMM to fund the top of the funnel just enough to feed the bottom.      “Don’t eat your seed corn.”    title: “Funnel Tradeoffs in Advertising: Optimizing Awareness, Conversion, and Retention” date: 2025-12-01 categories:         Artificial Intelligence     Machine Learning tags:     ad-tech     funnel-optimization     measurement            incrementality           ","categories": ["Artificial Intelligence","Machine Learning"],
        "tags": ["ad-tech","funnel-optimization","measurement","incrementality"],
